                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5250b3da-a86a-3ad5-8ddd-100a1633ca4f",
                        "entry_id": "2a75dce9-a592-36a2-b5ef-74c180ceb629",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. грубая, состоящая из волос какого-нибудь животного одежда монаха, отшельника, ведущего аскетическую жизнь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e6b5bc7-f051-4465-974c-7884b1bcc86e",
                                "sense_id": "5250b3da-a86a-3ad5-8ddd-100a1633ca4f",
                                "text": "Разделите одежды мои: епископу Афанасию отдайте одну милоть и подостланную подо мною одежду - она им мне дана новая и у меня обветшала, а епископу Серапиону отдайте другую милоть, власяницу возьмите себе."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "38e24d8a-5ee5-39d0-91a5-aa8f506e0e48",
                        "entry_id": "2a75dce9-a592-36a2-b5ef-74c180ceb629",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. темного цвета грубая ткань из козьей шерсти, в виде мешка, надевавшаяся в знак печали"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "51574f85-0ccd-4c97-b260-c7ada14fc03e",
                                "sense_id": "38e24d8a-5ee5-39d0-91a5-aa8f506e0e48",
                                "text": "Отправляясь на большие балы, она обнажалась гораздо больше пределов, дозволяемых приличием и модой, но говорили, что под низким декольте у неё всегда была надета власяница."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "38a0328d-e911-4479-ac7f-cb792d5df110",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a75dce9-a592-36a2-b5ef-74c180ceb629",
                        "target_lang_word": "cilice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cilice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cde44876-5ab7-312c-a4cf-806dd4f83a32",
                                        "entry_id": "9d1d7349-fce2-39d7-ac71-f692477db40c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A garment or undergarment made of coarse cloth or animal hair worn close to the skin used by members of various Christian traditions as a self-imposed means of penance (repentance) and mortification of the flesh."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afd0dd6e-9ca7-4b6d-b478-da13ac30f543",
                                                "sense_id": "cde44876-5ab7-312c-a4cf-806dd4f83a32",
                                                "text": "It was deemed meritorious to disfigure the body by neglect and filth, to extenuate it by fasting and watchfulness, to lacerate it with stripes, and to fret the wounds with cilices of horsehair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80d2ca38-bd88-33e3-8967-b44c3a26460c",
                                        "entry_id": "9d1d7349-fce2-39d7-ac71-f692477db40c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A leather strap studded with metallic barbs that cut into flesh as a constant reminder of Christ's suffering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in Opus Dei"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da90da08-016f-486d-a3d6-c795f52f326c",
                                                "sense_id": "80d2ca38-bd88-33e3-8967-b44c3a26460c",
                                                "text": "All she had done was give Teena a cilice, a barbed metal chain she was to tie around her thigh for two hours every day, and a discipline, a rope whip with knotted ends she was to use on her back when she prayed the Hail Mary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "39555a57-6d2c-46e7-b961-6b73ab93ed32",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a75dce9-a592-36a2-b5ef-74c180ceb629",
                        "target_lang_word": "hairshirt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hairshirt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35a68410-ed04-3b13-ba99-d3ea3eeb0b55",
                                        "entry_id": "cae088a3-7436-3022-9cdb-f1f2da7ec567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shirt made of haircloth; especially one worn by ascetics or the penitent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2935980c-f302-43bf-a41b-1fbb2aff667a",
                                                "sense_id": "35a68410-ed04-3b13-ba99-d3ea3eeb0b55",
                                                "text": "He is practically a total abstainer and I can affirm that he sleeps on a straw litter and eats the most Spartan food, cold dried grocer’s peas. He wears a hairshirt winter and summer and scourges himself every Saturday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe7bd329-9e21-3eef-a887-d4142060a5ca",
                                        "entry_id": "cae088a3-7436-3022-9cdb-f1f2da7ec567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of penitence and humility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ef3ff19-2c35-4755-90b3-85ceeb48abac",
                                                "sense_id": "fe7bd329-9e21-3eef-a887-d4142060a5ca",
                                                "text": "And when he went on to say, “The curse must be within ourselves,” Muir bequeathed us a hairshirt: the guilty conscience that plagues so many of us when we see what we are doing to the rest of nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hairshirt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e05c078c-701d-34e1-a370-98911a055cdb",
                                        "entry_id": "3037ad3f-e4a3-3456-8c88-34794fdeefca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Advocating or adopting a relatively ascetic lifestyle, especially for environmentalist reasons."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "relational"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45d4701e-4a8b-47e7-b181-8873075bf5f1",
                                                "sense_id": "e05c078c-701d-34e1-a370-98911a055cdb",
                                                "text": "The gloomy contentions of “hairshirt economists” who want more public and less private spending were assailed today by Robert W. Sarnoff, chairman of the National Broadcasting Company."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0de3f4b6-39bd-42df-b78d-b23a8398611e",
                                                "sense_id": "e05c078c-701d-34e1-a370-98911a055cdb",
                                                "text": "No hair-shirt ascetiscism, but far less consumerism, less shopping for the sake of shopping, less conspicuous consumption, less waste. There will be less trade, but it will be more judicious, and there will be more 'self-reliance' in energy, food and manufacturing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1eed162b-d240-4e74-b181-ddff7f9ab2d1",
                                                "sense_id": "e05c078c-701d-34e1-a370-98911a055cdb",
                                                "text": "Ireland – the \"poster child\" for the International Monetary Fund and EU's bailout programmes – endured its sixth hairshirt budget on Wednesday with the imposition of €2.5bn (£2bn) of cuts as its finance minister insisted the country is emerging from the fiscal crisis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f7b8612-4a4e-4029-909a-6c502842e7d7",
                                                "sense_id": "e05c078c-701d-34e1-a370-98911a055cdb",
                                                "text": "Boris Johnson has called on the government to drop its \"hair shirt, Stafford Cripps\" agenda as he outlined a seven-point growth plan for London involving building thousands of new homes and investment in major infrastructure projects."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
